{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals","id":1227167,"title":"A question about 2E alchemicals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Alchemical Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-13T10:12:11-07:00","id":1227167,"title":"A question about 2E alchemicals","content":"To anyone who actually played an alchemical in 2E, how often did you actually swap out individual charms or entire charm arrays?<br /> <br /> I'm in the process of trying to convert our beloved robots to 3E but I realized that in practice the charm slot/attunement cost setup of 2E may not have been as modular/adaptable as the book makes it out to be.<br /> <br /> Please no speculation. I'd like actual play experience only. Context of what type of game you were playing would also be very helpful. I'm trying to get a sense of how modular alchemicals need to be in play and whether I need to create systems to encourage/smooth out charm swapping or not. <br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for any feedback!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T13:35:50-07:00","id":1227208,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d have to dig into my records but I ran a fairly long Alchemicals game in 2e and I don\u2019t remember the players swapping things around too much. It was a game that took place in Nurad and I rembember trying to provide plenty of downtime between adventures for swapping and installing new charms, but I don\u2019t think they took much advantage of it. I might just be misremembering however. I\u2019ll ping some of them and see if they remember.<br /> <br /> I would say that I think charm swapping is a fundamental aspect of Alchemicals and should be encouraged, so I hope you come up with a good way to do it. Iirc, I think Vance has said that he doesn\u2019t think both slots and attunements are necessary.<br /> <br /> In any case, I\u2019ll ping my players about this and post again later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T13:44:41-07:00","id":1227212,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I appreciate the feedback. Once I've got something approaching a reasonably playable conversion, I'll try to post it to see what people think. (as a hint, I'm doubling down on the idea that Alchemical charms are artifacts)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T13:45:58-07:00","id":1227214,"title":"","content":"So, I've played a lot of Alchemicals, both 2E and 1E. I'll limit this to 2E since that's the specific question.<br /> <br /> In practice, the 5 hour waiting time per Charm swap usually proved prohibitive for the circumstances of our group. It made retooling for a specific purpose either on your own schedule or one you learn of reasonably ahead of time potentially viable - retools for either combat you plan to initiate on your own or a social event were both very reasonable. However, it felt like events forced us to change gears too quickly too often for most of our group to invest heavily in backup Charms, except for a few niche areas like specialized crafting loadouts. On top of that, any time you spend outside of a friendly pat/metropolis further limits the availability of refits - it doesn't matter if you have all the great tracking and survival Charms in the world if they're stuck back in town when your train breaks down.<br /> <br /> I'd say about half the group had no uninstalled Charms, most of the rest only having one or two that they either didn't plan on using often or that didn't really work out in play. I only remember one person bothering with two moderately different loadouts, and I remember it being an issue for him when the plan went off the rails even a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T15:00:23-07:00","id":1227244,"title":"","content":"I'm currently ST'ing a game of alchies in creation - they have a protocol user with the &quot;swap charms out in the field&quot; protocol<br /> <br /> That protocol is used often.<br /> <br /> arrays though? My players don't have any - yet - but I think that'll change once they finish their creation-side vat complex<br /> <br /> <br /> that said - all of my players used the background where you get access to extra spare charms at chargen - this generally makes swapping charms out a lot more attractive: all of them have what amounts to two different loadouts, though there is a lot of overlap between them<br /> <br /> my point is: to encourage more swapping, make sure someone in the circle/assembly has the protocol for instant swap-outs - and make sure they have something they want to switch between","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":588,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","user":"webkilla","date":". 06-13-2018, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T15:09:45-07:00","id":1227248,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2433_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2433\" data-vbnamecard=\"2433\">HighPriest</a> Thanks for the feedback! This is great stuff, though sadly kinda along the lines of what I was afraid of from 2E's way of doing things. While I did specify 2E, could you give me an idea of your 1E stuff as well? I've never played 1st addition myself so I'm not sure it would be as useful without the context but I'd love to hear your experiences there and what you felt was most enjoyable<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar588_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"588\" data-vbnamecard=\"588\">webkilla</a> Thanks for the feedback! Can you provide any context on what kinds of charms the players were swapping most often? Did they just swap out a couple of charms each or did they rebuild their whole characters for each situation? How do they get new charms if they're in creation? What about field improvements to things like attributes? Thanks in advance!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T16:56:05-07:00","id":1227272,"title":"","content":"When I played, I had premade layouts Combat/Social/Crafting, etc. that I was usually able to swap out. However, some, like the Dex Aug were never uninstalled.<br /> <br /> In our group there was very little swapping out a few charms. A couple other players had &quot;packages&quot; of 4 charms they treated like blocks, though not in arrays because there were some shared charms, that they would usually swap out when we had some downtime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T17:27:01-07:00","id":1227279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227248#post1227248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2433_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2433\" data-vbnamecard=\"2433\">HighPriest</a> While I did specify 2E, could you give me an idea of your 1E stuff as well? I've never played 1st addition myself so I'm not sure it would be as useful without the context but I'd love to hear your experiences there and what you felt was most enjoyable</div> </div> </div> </div>So 1E was very different, and it's clear that they were already trying to make Charm swapping more of a thing for 2E because the first edition method was far less reasonable. In 1E, Alchemicals had access to a Vats Background to reflect how much clout they had with a city's vat technicians. Without the background, any change - even swapping out Charms you already have - needed paperwork and a wait period of a month. If you maxed it out at 5 dots, you could get immediate service with a verbal request. Vats background also came with a number of Charms equal to the rating, so in theory characters who maxed it at character creation would have both little wait and a number of extra &quot;free&quot;-ish Charms.<br /> <br /> However, even at Vats 5, the actual swap then took a week, either to install new Charm slots or rearrange the existing slots. So the wait was quite long, even with the background maxed.<br /> <br /> It's obvious that 2E was already intended to be a streamlining of the process. I don't recall anyone ever using the system in 1E unless they really had to. Unless your game already has week long downtimes between most sessions, it just didn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T18:23:37-07:00","id":1227296,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2433_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2433\" data-vbnamecard=\"2433\">HighPriest</a> holy crap! Yeah I can see how that would be completely useless. I find 2E's system to be not very good at incentivizing charm swaps, though clearly people made <i>some </i>use of them. and it was certainly better than what 1E had <br /> <br /> I'm definitely catching themes of 'requires a lot of downtime' and 'only works when near cities with a VATS'<br /> <br /> I'm thinking there's room for a better/faster/more independent way to allow for players to swap stuff out without allowing mid-battle loadout changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T22:53:22-07:00","id":1227368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227212#post1227212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! I appreciate the feedback. Once I've got something approaching a reasonably playable conversion, I'll try to post it to see what people think. (as a hint, I'm doubling down on the idea that Alchemical charms are artifacts)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing going with an Artifact/Evocation model, where instead of having to actually attune to every charm, you attune to one &quot;base&quot; charm and then have evocations off of that? You could still have addons to the base that do need additional attunement, as a knob for balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T03:29:26-07:00","id":1227398,"title":"","content":"If you keep the &quot;has to be committed using personal essence&quot; part of installation you might be able to get away with simply letting them summon them wherever they are, since peripheral refills first and that would make it hard to swap them out in the middle of a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T04:47:37-07:00","id":1227407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227208#post1227208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d have to dig into my records but I ran a fairly long Alchemicals game in 2e and I don\u2019t remember the players swapping things around too much. It was a game that took place in Nurad and I rembember trying to provide plenty of downtime between adventures for swapping and installing new charms, but I don\u2019t think they took much advantage of it. I might just be misremembering however. I\u2019ll ping some of them and see if they remember.<br /> <br /> I would say that I think charm swapping is a fundamental aspect of Alchemicals and should be encouraged, so I hope you come up with a good way to do it. Iirc, I think Vance has said that he doesn\u2019t think both slots and attunements are necessary.<br /> <br /> In any case, I\u2019ll ping my players about this and post again later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do recall <i>Beacon</i> doing a little bit of shifting around from time to time between a full combat set and mixing in a few social Charms, but for the most part she stuck with combat gear because it was good enough for physical labor and she had to be ever cautious of the threat of the Void.<br /> <br /> Came down to what was going on in that specific game, rather than a general statement on the design of Alchemicals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/172-elohteebee","name":"ElOhTeeBee","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T05:04:31-07:00","id":1227408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227248#post1227248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2433_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2433\" data-vbnamecard=\"2433\">HighPriest</a> Thanks for the feedback! This is great stuff, though sadly kinda along the lines of what I was afraid of from 2E's way of doing things. While I did specify 2E, could you give me an idea of your 1E stuff as well? I've never played 1st addition myself so I'm not sure it would be as useful without the context but I'd love to hear your experiences there and what you felt was most enjoyable<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar588_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"588\" data-vbnamecard=\"588\">webkilla</a> Thanks for the feedback! Can you provide any context on what kinds of charms the players were swapping most often? Did they just swap out a couple of charms each or did they rebuild their whole characters for each situation? How do they get new charms if they're in creation? What about field improvements to things like attributes? Thanks in advance!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Example:<br /> <br /> A crafting-monkey alchy who likes to swap between the mega-ton piston hammer charm and his industrial survival frame - one is for risky tunneling, one is for rightous suck beatings.<br /> <br /> Another is the assemble's medical and social specialist - he swaps between his medic/combat charms and all of his mind-probe charm (his form of social combat is rather... non-consentual)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T05:09:25-07:00","id":1227409,"title":"","content":"If you cut out all the tedious faffing around then having to change out at the vats could sort of work like it would in a videogame. <br /> <br /> You get a mission, you open the options menu to reconfigure stuff, you head out, and once you're done you come back. <br /> <br /> Probably need to introduce some sort of portable vats complex or something for away-missions. If everyone is taking the charm-swapping protocol that says to me that it should be a standard feature instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T07:00:23-07:00","id":1227426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227296#post1227296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2433_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2433\" data-vbnamecard=\"2433\">HighPriest</a> holy crap! Yeah I can see how that would be completely useless. I find 2E's system to be not very good at incentivizing charm swaps, though clearly people made <i>some </i>use of them. and it was certainly better than what 1E had<br /> <br /> I'm definitely catching themes of 'requires a lot of downtime' and 'only works when near cities with a VATS'<br /> <br /> I'm thinking there's room for a better/faster/more independent way to allow for players to swap stuff out without allowing mid-battle loadout changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have access to Shards of the Exalted Dream? Because the Modern Shard had a very different origin for Alchemicals and they had new rules to reflect that. You might find looking at those useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T07:32:08-07:00","id":1227432,"title":"","content":"Swapping out a charmset needs to take like an hour, tops. Something you can easily just skip. <br /> <br /> Upgrading attributes or essence can maybe stretch to a day. If training times show up it should represent how long a new charm or the upgrades required for a strength dot take to build while the alchie is doing something else. <br /> <br /> Seriously whoever thought it was a good idea to require up to a <i>month</i> of downtime before you could use the primary feature that sets alchemical charms apart from the other exalted's needs to be slapped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T07:49:27-07:00","id":1227435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227368#post1227368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm guessing going with an Artifact/Evocation model, where instead of having to actually attune to every charm, you attune to one &quot;base&quot; charm and then have evocations off of that? You could still have addons to the base that do need additional attunement, as a knob for balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty close. Essentially my alchemicals have a caste and a favored material and they can buy evocations for them at favored costs. Caste determines anima powers and which set of three attributes that become your primary attributes for character building. Favored determines the secondary three. Using the 2E set of attribute to material associations each material has three attributes. In the case of overlap (both jade and soulsteel have stamina for instance) you can buy that attribute up to 6 at char gen. Otherwise the attribute cap is 5+ (essence/2 round down).<br /> <br /> Certain charms that are central to every champion and possibly meta-evocations will be available as straight charm purchases. My conceit there is that the alchemical herself is an N/A artifact that has certain evocations built off of it. So far these include the excellencies and ox-body. <br /> <br /> To facilitate swapping and modding of your 'charm' set, I think that at most it would require minor surgery at a difficulty of the artifact rating that you're installing and impossible to fail (failure takes longer, a botch takes longer <i>and</i> does a level of health damage so there's still some incentive to have a professional install them) and new charms can only be constructed at the VATS. Furthermore, I'm thinking to avoid a sunk cost type situation like with evocations, they'll be able to essentially buy a number of favored evocations that can be selected from any installed favored charm and rearranged every time you install/uninstall a charm. So if you decide you want to drop your piston-driven megaton hammer (which is now an artifact smashfist with evocations) and want to install a different favored charm in its place you can reassign the evocations you bought for PDMH in the new charm. I want to avoid having giant pools of xp spent on evocations that are only available when they're installed. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227432#post1227432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swapping out a charmset needs to take like an hour, tops. Something you can easily just skip.<br /> <br /> Upgrading attributes or essence can maybe stretch to a day. If training times show up it should represent how long a new charm or the upgrades required for a strength dot take to build while the alchie is doing something else.<br /> <br /> <b>Seriously whoever thought it was a good idea to require up to a <i>month</i> of downtime before you could use the primary feature that sets alchemical charms apart from the other exalted's needs to be slapped</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>So much agreed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T07:58:03-07:00","id":1227439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227426#post1227426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you have access to Shards of the Exalted Dream? Because the Modern Shard had a very different origin for Alchemicals and they had new rules to reflect that. You might find looking at those useful.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ya - cyborg lunars who technomorph - a very cool spin on the concept","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T11:55:58-07:00","id":1227485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227432#post1227432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swapping out a charmset needs to take like an hour, tops. Something you can easily just skip. <br /> <br /> Upgrading attributes or essence can maybe stretch to a day. If training times show up it should represent how long a new charm or the upgrades required for a strength dot take to build while the alchie is doing something else. <br /> <br /> Seriously whoever thought it was a good idea to require up to a <i>month</i> of downtime before you could use the primary feature that sets alchemical charms apart from the other exalted's needs to be slapped.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree that a month is too long, I do think it\u2019s possible for the refit time to be too short. I mean, if an Alchemical can just swap out their entire combat charmset with a reflexive action or even a normal action, it becomes a more complicated version of the Aura mechanic and stops feeling like much of a drawback. <br /> <br /> I get that an hour isn\u2019t the same thing as a combat action ....but, in social situations, it can be. You could have an associate filibuster the grand assembly or move for a recess or be fashionably late, any of which could be represented as just one \u201cinfluence round\u201d and give you enough time to swap your entire loadout as needed.<br /> <br /> Another aspect of this is that Alchemical charms are frequently multifunctional and might be useful in many areas ...but, the more useful it is, the less often you need to swap it out. If you want people to swap more, giving them more reason to do so might be just as important as lowering the barriers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T12:03:01-07:00","id":1227486,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... What if each Alchemical had an \u201cEmergency Swap Beacon\u201d that would let them swap out all the charms they wanted instantly.... but it burned out after one use until repaired at your vat complex, and a normal refit takes, say, 15 minutes per charm, up to a maximum of 8 hours or a flat four hours?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T05:58:54-07:00","id":1227631,"title":"","content":"The problem I found with charm slots was that there just wasn't enough incentive to swap. I've seen Alchemical players shoot down the idea of having a social build on the logic that they're basically a living warship and a warship doesn't remove its guns because it's serving a ceremonial function and I'm not sure to what extent that was influenced by 2e paranoia combat or the Autochthonia setting.<br /> <br /> I think their charmset should have an element of deliberate incompatibility i.e. having most of their soak enhancers count as armour coupled with some of their better movement charms being incompatible with armour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T08:07:08-07:00","id":1227661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227631#post1227631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem I found with charm slots was that there just wasn't enough incentive to swap. I've seen Alchemical players shoot down the idea of having a social build on the logic that they're basically a living warship and a warship doesn't remove its guns because it's serving a ceremonial function and I'm not sure to what extent that was influenced by 2e paranoia combat or the Autochthonia setting.<br /> <br /> I think their charmset should have an element of deliberate incompatibility i.e. having most of their soak enhancers count as armour coupled with some of their better movement charms being incompatible with armour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... On one hand I know what you mean, but I think I disagree on the execution.<br /> <br /> I think it's problematic to deliberately build multiple incompatibilities into the charmset. To some extent they'll be present regardless since I'm going with attunement costs to control charm installation #'s, but honestly if a player wants to install one charm and buy up dozens of evocations for that one charm then I don't think that's a bad thing. All it means is that they're deliberately limiting their character.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I should stress that a Champion is less like a piece of hardware and more like a computer. A computer is infinitely variable based solely on the programs and peripherals installed whereas hardware is limited by what it's built for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T08:49:35-07:00","id":1227677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227485#post1227485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that an hour isn\u2019t the same thing as a combat action ....but, in social situations, it can be. You could have an associate filibuster the grand assembly or move for a recess or be fashionably late, any of which could be represented as just one \u201cinfluence round\u201d and give you enough time to swap your entire loadout as needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds a lot more like a feature than a bug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T09:12:25-07:00","id":1227684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227661#post1227661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's problematic to deliberately build multiple incompatibilities into the charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say only where it's unclear and forced. The signature mechanic is an incompatibility built into the Dragon-Blooded charmset and they're better for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T09:33:27-07:00","id":1227687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227684#post1227684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say only where it's unclear and forced. The signature mechanic is an incompatibility built into the Dragon-Blooded charmset and they're better for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To a lesser degree it\u2019s also the main purpose of the aura mechanic which... Well personally I\u2019m ambivalent about but it definitely could have been worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T10:56:47-07:00","id":1227702,"title":"","content":"This is true. Plus alchemicals are supposed to be as close to the Dragon Bloods as the celestial tier gets (and the distinction is more fuzzy than ever in this edition)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T12:08:10-07:00","id":1227712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227296#post1227296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> holy crap! Yeah I can see how that would be completely useless. I find 2E's system to be not very good at incentivizing charm swaps, though clearly people made <i>some </i>use of them. and it was certainly better than what 1E had <br /> <br /> I'm definitely catching themes of 'requires a lot of downtime' and 'only works when near cities with a VATS'<br /> <br /> I'm thinking there's room for a better/faster/more independent way to allow for players to swap stuff out without allowing mid-battle loadout changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to that. I would suggest offering free combos. And maybe shorter attribute learning times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T12:09:23-07:00","id":1227714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227677#post1227677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds a lot more like a feature than a bug.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s a consideration. Really everything here is something to consider, including \u201cgiving Alchemicals reconfigurable charms is actually a bad idea and we shouldn\u2019t do it again.\u201d<br /> <br /> Honestly, it might be worth going back and asking \u201cwhy are we giving Alchemicals reconfiguable charms in the first place?\u201d<br /> <br /> The answers I\u2019ve come up with so far for that are as follows:<br /> <br /> * It serves as an external power check on Alchemicals, so that they cannot use all their charms at once, which helps set their rough position on the power scale without having to give them entirely useless charms.<br /> * It feels techy and cool, so it helps set the atmosphere and make Alchemicals distinctive from other Exalted.<br /> * It helps tie Alchemicals into the industrial infrastructure and society of the Eight Nations, making everything more cohesive.<br /> <br /> And here are some fundamental issues with it:<br /> <br /> * On the other hand, it can make characters feel less distinctive, since they don\u2019t necessarily have iconic charms anymore.<br /> * Or a character who does have a favorite set of charms might just skip using the mechanic entirely, which will either make their character much less effective overall or simply point out that the mechanic is unnecessary.<br /> * Unless abilities and attributes are equally discounted as charms, it might be difficult to get enough dice together to really make use of the swapping mechanic.<br /> * Most players are used to creating a team of specialists who each have a particular skill that enables the party as a whole to handle a wide range of tasks. Suddenly being able to have an entire team of diplomancers might cause problems and complaints of \u201cyou\u2019re getting into my niche\u201d without explicitly examining the idea.<br /> <br /> For that last one, designing in fairly obvious and somewhat narrow builds that work well in concert might be a good idea. Like a good build for Reading Intentions that can give ammo to the Persuader build, while an Inspirer build helps set the mood in the background to give extra bonuses to the others. Since it\u2019s difficult to do three things at once, it can be useful to have those as three different people, so setting things up like that in the charms might help bring that out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 06-15-2018, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T13:07:04-07:00","id":1227733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227714#post1227714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s a consideration. Really everything here is something to consider, including \u201cgiving Alchemicals reconfigurable charms is actually a bad idea and we shouldn\u2019t do it again.\u201d<br /> <br /> Honestly, it might be worth going back and asking \u201cwhy are we giving Alchemicals reconfiguable charms in the first place?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about what if charm sets/load outs were really different bodies the Alchemical could use? Like Altered Carbon or Eclipse Phase. The Alchemical could be just a brain and Essence that can be transferred between bodies it owns.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T13:31:38-07:00","id":1227738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227712#post1227712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want to that. I would suggest offering free combos. And maybe shorter attribute learning times.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'm going to go with 'training times' for attributes requiring that amount of time to construct for you in a VATS, but the actual installation is an hour or less once it's done. In 3E you can train multiple traits at the same time if they're related (running drills could train up athletics, strength and stamina at the same time). I want similar use out of the VATs technicians as well.<br /> <br /> Combos, and the need for them, aren't a thing in 3E any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T14:04:10-07:00","id":1227747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227714#post1227714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s a consideration. Really everything here is something to consider, including \u201cgiving Alchemicals reconfigurable charms is actually a bad idea and we shouldn\u2019t do it again.\u201d<br /> <br /> Honestly, it might be worth going back and asking \u201cwhy are we giving Alchemicals reconfiguable charms in the first place?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely worth considering in any 3rd edition port. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227714#post1227714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The answers I\u2019ve come up with so far for that are as follows:<br /> <br /> * It serves as an external power check on Alchemicals, so that they cannot use all their charms at once, which helps set their rough position on the power scale without having to give them entirely useless charms.<br /> * It feels techy and cool, so it helps set the atmosphere and make Alchemicals distinctive from other Exalted.<br /> * It helps tie Alchemicals into the industrial infrastructure and society of the Eight Nations, making everything more cohesive.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd also add that properly implemented it may give some of the Batman feel to Alchemicals. IE: Given time to prepare for every situation I'm unstopable.<br /> <br /> Your cons I'm going to examine one at a time.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227714#post1227714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And here are some fundamental issues with it:<br /> <br /> * On the other hand, it can make characters feel less distinctive, since they don\u2019t necessarily have iconic charms anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is a problem if you treat alchemical charms the way 3E treats artifacts. Every Champion who installs Piston-Driven Megaton Hammer is going to have a slightly different take on it, flavored by what caste and personality they are. It does raise questions of how can more than one champion even have PDMH since artifacts aren't normally replicable but I'm working around that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227714#post1227714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Or a character who does have a favorite set of charms might just skip using the mechanic entirely, which will either make their character much less effective overall or simply point out that the mechanic is unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because one player chooses to specialize does not negate the advantages of charm swaps for other players. A lunar can choose to stay in one form forever (including human) and that's not a problem. Charm design should encourage different playstyles, not enforce them.<br /> <br /> I'm perfectly fine with a player installing a single charm and then building an evocation tree off of it if that's the only thing they want to be able to do. Alchemicals can't dip into charm trees to round out a build the way solars who focus on evocations can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227714#post1227714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Unless abilities and attributes are equally discounted as charms, it might be difficult to get enough dice together to really make use of the swapping mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean by this? Are you suggesting that the charms be mostly divorced from attribute/ability combos or that alchemicals should be able to swap around their attributes/abilities at need? Or do you mean something else that I'm not getting?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227714#post1227714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Most players are used to creating a team of specialists who each have a particular skill that enables the party as a whole to handle a wide range of tasks. Suddenly being able to have an entire team of diplomancers might cause problems and complaints of \u201cyou\u2019re getting into my niche\u201d without explicitly examining the idea.<br /> <br /> For that last one, designing in fairly obvious and somewhat narrow builds that work well in concert might be a good idea. Like a good build for Reading Intentions that can give ammo to the Persuader build, while an Inspirer build helps set the mood in the background to give extra bonuses to the others. Since it\u2019s difficult to do three things at once, it can be useful to have those as three different people, so setting things up like that in the charms might help bring that out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you mean here, but Alchemicals are the splat most useful for bypassing niches and niche protection entirely. I find in the 3E game I'm playing in currently most scenes have one or two players come to the forefront and the rest don't have much to do. The bruiser is the combat monkey, while the Twilight has almost no combat skills at all. To me, the ability to swap out competencies should allow most characters to have <i>something</i> to do in most situations. At least that's what I'm hoping... The trick is balancing attunement costs and charm purchases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T20:19:16-07:00","id":1227805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227747#post1227747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think this is a problem if you treat alchemical charms the way 3E treats artifacts. Every Champion who installs Piston-Driven Megaton Hammer is going to have a slightly different take on it, flavored by what caste and personality they are. It does raise questions of how can more than one champion even have PDMH since artifacts aren't normally replicable but I'm working around that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider that artifacts are replicable at their most basic level. I mean, there are thousands of Daiklaves and all of them have the same basic power to be a &quot;Giant Anime Sword that can be swung around like a Feather.&quot; They all get different powers beyond that and none of them are exactly the same, but there are nevertheless lots of basic categories of artifact that all do basically the same things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227747#post1227747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what you mean by this? Are you suggesting that the charms be mostly divorced from attribute/ability combos or that alchemicals should be able to swap around their attributes/abilities at need? Or do you mean something else that I'm not getting?</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm saying is that, if Enthusiastic Agile Mechanic, who has Cha 3, Manip 1, and App 3 and zero dots in social abilities because her player spent everything on getting Craft 5 three times, tries to install a social suite...well, assuming she can meet the minimums, she's going to only have 3 to 6 dice on all her rolls and will likely still be a poor diplomat, even if she can get double 9s on Read Intentions rolls and gets +3 charm dice on all social rolls for a scene.<br /> <br /> 2e solved this problem with the Fourth through Sixth (Attribute) Augmentations, so that, if Mechanic was the only diplomat they could send, they could load her up with a bunch of 4th or 5th Augs to boost her social stats to peak human levels (or beyond) and a bunch of 6th Augs to boost her effective Presence and Socialize ratings both to 5, and then give her a nice social suite on top of that. It's expensive, but it can be done.<br /> <br /> That said, once you've done that, does the character still feel like the same person?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 06-15-2018, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T22:21:23-07:00","id":1227815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227805#post1227805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2e solved this problem with the Fourth through Sixth (Attribute) Augmentations, so that, if Mechanic was the only diplomat they could send, they could load her up with a bunch of 4th or 5th Augs to boost her social stats to peak human levels (or beyond) and a bunch of 6th Augs to boost her effective Presence and Socialize ratings both to 5, and then give her a nice social suite on top of that. It's expensive, but it can be done.<br /> <br /> That said, once you've done that, does the character still feel like the same person?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlike other exalts, I would say yes. The attributes didn't really change the character. Rather they came from external tools. You had voice modulators which made you sound more alluring. Chassis augments that made you more intimidating. The character could still be the same though. I feel like a lot of people didn't take advantage of the fact that an alchemical unlike other exalts exist to change purpose more than any other exalt and that multiple exalts could hold multiple roles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T03:26:28-07:00","id":1227837,"title":"","content":"I liked alchies being able to just install skills. Hope that sticks around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T11:24:08-07:00","id":1227877,"title":"","content":"Something else to consider is xp costs vs. how easy you want to enable going from \u201cmiddling mortal\u201d to \u201cskilled mortal/basic exalt\u201d to \u201ccompentent exalt\u201d to \u201cbest exalt ever.\u201d<br /> <br /> The example I listed above with Mechanic, assuming she already had 15 charm slots, ends up costing 90 xp for 15 social charms and gets you effective Cha 4, Manip 3, App 4, 1st Cha and Manip Excellencies, effective Presence and Socialize values of 5, and 5 misc social charms. This should be enough to put her in the high side of \u201cskilled mortal/basic exalt\u201d or the low end of \u201ccomptent exalt\u201d depending. <br /> <br /> Now, iirc, going from 1 to 3 in an Attribute costs 12 points and going from 3 to 4 costs 12 points and going from 0 to 5 in an ability costs 33 points. So doing the above normally costs 102xp just for the stat bonuses, which cost the Alchemical 60xp. So there\u2019s a significant advantage there.<br /> <br /> I will also grant that it\u2019s something of an extreme case where a character decides that they want to go from \u201cthis is my dump stat\u201d to \u201cactually pretty good at this,\u201d and in most cases it\u2019ll usually be someone picking up a few extra charms to round out a secondary competency or just not suck at their third (say buying 4th Manip twice and a Guile booster so they can stand in the back and not give the game away while the actual diplomats talk) which can be done pretty cheaply and thus fairly easily, though it still takes a bit of advance planning (or keeping 18 xp banked for emergencies).<br /> <br /> But... Well, if you really wanna enable the \u201cI can deal with anything at all, provided I can get a day to prepare\u201d thing, you might wanna include a few emergency options (with significant downsides) that let an Alchemical install a big chunk of charms they haven\u2019t actually purchased yet. Maybe they can borrow the unused charms of other Alchemicals, but it creates a bunch of issues and rapidly increasing penalties if they keep them installed for more than a day. Maybe they can take out a loan from the state and pay it back later.<br /> <br /> Something to consider anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T11:54:41-07:00","id":1227881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227877#post1227877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something else to consider is xp costs vs. how easy you want to enable going from \u201cmiddling mortal\u201d to \u201cskilled mortal/basic exalt\u201d to \u201ccompentent exalt\u201d to \u201cbest exalt ever.\u201d<br /> <br /> The example I listed above with Mechanic, assuming she already had 15 charm slots, ends up costing 90 xp for 15 social charms and gets you effective Cha 4, Manip 3, App 4, 1st Cha and Manip Excellencies, effective Presence and Socialize values of 5, and 5 misc social charms. This should be enough to put her in the high side of \u201cskilled mortal/basic exalt\u201d or the low end of \u201ccomptent exalt\u201d depending.<br /> <br /> Now, iirc, going from 1 to 3 in an Attribute costs 12 points and going from 3 to 4 costs 12 points and going from 0 to 5 in an ability costs 33 points. So doing the above normally costs 102xp just for the stat bonuses, which cost the Alchemical 60xp. So there\u2019s a significant advantage there.<br /> <br /> I will also grant that it\u2019s something of an extreme case where a character decides that they want to go from \u201cthis is my dump stat\u201d to \u201cactually pretty good at this,\u201d and in most cases it\u2019ll usually be someone picking up a few extra charms to round out a secondary competency or just not suck at their third (say buying 4th Manip twice and a Guile booster so they can stand in the back and not give the game away while the actual diplomats talk) which can be done pretty cheaply and thus fairly easily, though it still takes a bit of advance planning (or keeping 18 xp banked for emergencies).<br /> <br /> But... Well, if you really wanna enable the \u201cI can deal with anything at all, provided I can get a day to prepare\u201d thing, you might wanna include a few emergency options (with significant downsides) that let an Alchemical install a big chunk of charms they haven\u2019t actually purchased yet. Maybe they can borrow the unused charms of other Alchemicals, but it creates a bunch of issues and rapidly increasing penalties if they keep them installed for more than a day. Maybe they can take out a loan from the state and pay it back later.<br /> <br /> Something to consider anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> good point<br /> <br /> I would argue that this is partially where arrays come in - favorite or commonly used loadouts<br /> <br /> In the alchy game I currently ST my players all have 8 or 9 slots, but only swap out one or two charms regularly for each them.<br /> <br /> I guess it depends on how far into the game you get with alchies - most of my players are at the state where they're saving up to hit essence 4 before diving big into high-end charms, or other specialties","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T09:38:01-07:00","id":1228057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1227631#post1227631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem I found with charm slots was that there just wasn't enough incentive to swap. I've seen Alchemical players shoot down the idea of having a social build on the logic that they're basically a living warship and a warship doesn't remove its guns because it's serving a ceremonial function and I'm not sure to what extent that was influenced by 2e paranoia combat or the Autochthonia setting.<br /> <br /> I think their charmset should have an element of deliberate incompatibility i.e. having most of their soak enhancers count as armour coupled with some of their better movement charms being incompatible with armour.</div> </div> </div> </div>I went back and read over the 2ed Alchemicals a little bit, and the biggest encouragement for charms swapping is the ease of having more charms for the cost than you have slots. You could buy an extra charm from starting for 1 bonus OR background point. One could make a character with 25 EXTRA CHARMS from character gen. Even with experience a Charm slot costs same as a charm (a little less if deidcated). So do you want a charm and a slot to put it in, or two charms to swap out with another option?<br /> <br /> Maybe like Artifacts have Evocation limits unless 5dots or N/A, Alchemicals have Charm Slot maximums at certain Essence Levels. Since they were based on Personal Essence levels some anyways that was still true, but obvious spelling out of it may be better for 1st time players.<br /> <br /> Going Evocation style sounds like a good idea, though i ponder what you can do to keep the Alchemical charms from feeling too much like Artifacts themselves. A starmetal slayer khatar made to wipe memories vs. a mind spike mounted at the wrist, what is the difference? Keeping some Abyssal from ripping it off and using it should have some difference<br /> (Beyond the gory medicine check to shove it in his own body for the mind spike)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T10:17:51-07:00","id":1228062,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that alchy charms cost essence to have installed...<br /> <br /> sure you can have 20 charm slots with active charms in them - but... you will be sorely lacking in essence to use those charms<br /> <br /> and I've never seen any alchy player go ham on extra charms at chargen like that - artifacts, using bonus points on extra ability or attribute points, or other backgrounds - that's far more common<br /> <br /> I for one do NOT like the idea of alchy charm evocations - it would mess with the sub-module system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":588,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","user":"webkilla","date":". 06-17-2018, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T11:00:55-07:00","id":1228070,"title":"","content":"I think if anything it would <i>eat</i> the sub-module system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T14:47:21-07:00","id":1228120,"title":"","content":"yeah, no matter what system we get homebrewed or official it's not gonna look very much like 2E. Arrays are based on combos, and combos are <i>dead</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T15:02:11-07:00","id":1228123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1228120#post1228120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah, no matter what system we get homebrewed or official it's not gonna look very much like 2E. Arrays are based on combos, and combos are <i>dead</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yes and no - I would argue that arrays still have a justification: they reduce the installation cost by a quarter. An array with charms that cost 12 motes to keep running, will only got 9 now.<br /> <br /> If anything I'd suggest making arrays free - its 'just' linking a series of charms you've already paid for. It's what I do in my game.<br /> <br /> <br /> and Elfive - yes, it'd eat the sub-module system - but the thing about evocations is that its about mastering a thing and learning its deeper powers. With alchy charms, sub-modules are all about building onto it, adding something there wasn't there before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T16:37:21-07:00","id":1228143,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for arrays that basically changed their purpose entirely.<br /> <br /> Actually it was to help with the &quot;nobody switches charms&quot; problem.<br /> <br /> Basically it worked like this: An array lets you put more than one charm into a single slot. Bigger arrays would take up more slots, with my completely untested value being charms/3, rounded up. The downside was that activating an array also deactivated an equal number of slots to what it took up, and you could only have one active at a time.<br /> <br /> The idea was that this would incentivize carrying two different arrays you could swap between. Expanding your overall charm capacity while restricting which ones you could use at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T19:42:27-07:00","id":1228191,"title":"","content":"Ahh, the problem with slots. I can tell you this was a pretty huge problem in my 2e game, people almost never switched out charms. People almost never bought charms they didn't have slots for either, it simply wasn't worth the XP in most cases. You did see charms getting re-configured, changing out specialties and such, but people pretty much stuck to a core set of abilities that defined them and didn't play around much beyond that. There might be an exception for one or two players where, for one of their slots, they'd shift between the one or two spare charms until they ended up buying additional slots.<br /> <br /> There's a good reason for this too, your character's potency in crisis situations stems from their invested XP. You can diversify and have a lot of options, but that means you just spend most of your time without access to a sizable chunk of your invested XP. Or you can continue to invest in submodules or say martial arts/protocol weaving where you don't have to sacrifice personal potential for the illusion of versatility.<br /> <br /> All of that went into consideration when I did my 3e rebuild: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069674-homebrew-ex3-creation-gate-total-alchemical-re-write\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...mical-re-write</a><br /> <br /> Here's what we did: Alchemicals buy &quot;core&quot; charms that becomes part of them, these don't get the same kinds of mild discount that previous versions did. Their slots could be filled with anything at no XP cost, though each charm had a much heftier install cost against your personal motes, up to 4 motes each that only cost more with sub modules included. This encouraged players to try out new things and determine if it was a situational need or they wanted to establish that capability as part of their core identity down the road. It also let them practice with new submodules and gain the versatility that they were intended to from the design perspective. Even still, some players hardly swapped things out but that lack of preperation came back to bite them later on. There's a bit of a learning curve too, overzealous players would load up and discover that only having 3 motes of personal essence lead to a lot of problems with constantly flaring animas, so it was always sort of a balancing act to find that right sweet spot for whatever loadout they wanted to go with: Trying to be social or stealthy kept the installed charms lite while going to war where there wasn't social/circumstantial consequences to glowing like a beacon would have people armed to the teeth. I don't see this as a problem though, rather a design feature that encompasses what we thought players really wanted !<br /> <br /> Anyway, I spent WAY too much time doing charm design and balance, feel free to utilize <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069674-homebrew-ex3-creation-gate-total-alchemical-re-write\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...mical-re-write</a> wholesale or adapt the charms to suit your purposes. These were developed to be celestial tier without a bunch of time consuming dice tricks. Some mechanics were lifted wholesale from the 3e core book because interesting mechanics are always more fun than dice adders. Plus we went with the adage of: There should be more meaningful options available than one player could ever take, that way two players can take the same things while still being distinct. The Essence levels were scaled to: 1-3, typical alchemical champion; 4-5 is an alchemical colossus and anything beyond that gets into the municipal level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1759-kawaiiwolf","name":"kawaiiwolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1759_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T02:33:00-07:00","id":1228235,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the unused XP is an issue.<br /> <br /> Maybe one solution would be to take a &quot;how do I hold all these charms?&quot; approach. Chargen, you get enough charms to fill your slots, plus a bunch extra. Buy a slot? 2 free charms. Go up in essence? Free charms. <br /> <br /> Just make it literally impossible to have enough slots to use every charm you own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T08:45:15-07:00","id":1228310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1228235#post1228235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the unused XP is an issue.<br /> <br /> Maybe one solution would be to take a &amp;quot;how do I hold all these charms?&amp;quot; approach. Chargen, you get enough charms to fill your slots, plus a bunch extra. Buy a slot? 2 free charms. Go up in essence? Free charms. <br /> <br /> Just make it literally impossible to have enough slots to use every charm you own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now this is some proper 3rd edition style thinking. I like it, the team working on things for the Alchemical is always coming up with something new to try while the Alchemical is doing their own thing. Not sure how to reconcile that with the automatic essence upgrades as well, but I'm sure fiddling with it a bit could help.<br /> <br /> The other angle i can think of would be the encouragement of swapping through exclusive charms plugging into specific slots. Obviously this can make it tough to make particular builds. Very rough draft thought: all charms are external items, so maybe the body has a max slot spaces number at each Essence level. Either sort by major body zone or some fantasy chakra spreadsheet. Higher Essence improves space compatability (or increases size of Exalt). Get them more charms than slots right from the start so they have the options from the start, and the encouragement for switchout style gameplay","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T09:20:26-07:00","id":1228312,"title":"","content":"Yeah, maybe not essence. Attributes? That makes more sense.<br /> <br /> Charm slot slots are a bit close to installation costs, which he devs have said they might drop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T11:21:01-07:00","id":1228335,"title":"","content":"Personally, I\u2019d just straight up drop either Slots or Installation Costs. They do slightly different things, but their main functions are similar enough that you probably don\u2019t need both. Of the two, I\u2019d probably drop Slots and just say that you can install everything you can power.<br /> <br /> If you want to be able to swap things out quickly, you could say that you could install some non-powered charms (which give a penalty for each extra charm) and then allow the Alchemical to switch around what\u2019s powered with an action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T15:36:58-07:00","id":1228397,"title":"","content":"I believe the Devs have stated that they're only going to do one of slots or attunement, not both. <br /> <br /> Personally I prefer to drop slots as well. <br /> <br /> I wonder if it's possible to grant a bonus of some sort from charms you don't have installed so that there's no problem of useless, sunk xp... I'll think on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T16:36:58-07:00","id":1228409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1228397#post1228397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the Devs have stated that they're only going to do one of slots or attunement, not both. <br /> <br /> Personally I prefer to drop slots as well. <br /> <br /> I wonder if it's possible to grant a bonus of some sort from charms you don't have installed so that there's no problem of useless, sunk xp... I'll think on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could allow them to recycle charms they definitely don\u2019t want anymore, but I wouldn\u2019t put that in as a specific game mechanic unless you want to have people recycling charms regularly so they don\u2019t need to spend xp on the new stuff they want. If so, I\u2019d definitely make recycling take a month or more, to ensure there was incentive to keep some charms ready on \u201cstandby\u201d instead of just being able to reuse the same 60 xp over and over again as you swapped jobs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T14:37:44-07:00","id":1229235,"title":"","content":"How would people feel about this setup: <br /> <br /> All alchemical charms are artifacts with evocations. Like regular artifacts they have attunement costs and a theme based on material composition and function. Most of these physical 'charms' have attunement bonuses similar to artifacts. <br /> <br /> Unlike normal artifacts they need to be installed surgically and they only function while attuned to an alchemical. <br /> <br /> Champions themselves have the following abilities with regards to alchemical charms: whenever they drop an attunement, they save the number of evocation purchases they've made form the charm. Then when they attune a different charm, they can invest those same evocations into the new charm. For instance, if you're got a champion with Thousand Courtesan calculations with 5 evocations, you can drop TCC and attune Piston Driven Megaton Hammer instead and instantly buy up 5 evocations out of PDMH evocation tree. You'd essentially have a pool of purchased evocations that you can allocate to different charms. <br /> <br /> Now this takes care of the problem of xp being sunk into evocations that are unavailable but what about the charms themselves? I have two possible ways to deal with this:<br /> Either 1) alchemical charms are requisitioned from a VATS but do not cost xp to purchase or install. They'd be limited purely by the cost of attunement vs their limited mote pool. <br /> OR 2) most alchemical charms can be installed without being attuned and you still get the base 'attunement' bonus but you cannot use any evocations form them and perhaps some charms would impose a penalty if not attuned if they're physically unwieldy or potentially hazardous or something (voidtech still imposes gremlin syndrome for instance, attuned or not).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T19:07:34-07:00","id":1229272,"title":"","content":"If the bulk of an alchemical's charmset is in the form of floating evocations then you could probably get away with making the charms themselves free. <br /> <br /> Or maybe you could make it a little like essence and give them a free charm for every X experience they spend or something. <br /> <br /> Although really you might get away with letting them buy the charms. It's a bit like regular evocations. You're spending exp on powers you might not necessarily have access to all the time. People are pretty happy to do that wrt artifacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T20:48:47-07:00","id":1229287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1229272#post1229272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although really you might get away with letting them buy the charms. It's a bit like regular evocations. You're spending exp on powers you might not necessarily have access to all the time. People are pretty happy to do that wrt artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true. <br /> <br /> I suspect it might be slightly different feeling though. As a solar or dragon blood using a weapon with evocations you may be denied access to them by being disarmed, but you always have your native charms to fall back on. With the paradigm of all charms being artifacts, it's not external factors denying their use but personal choice and circumstances. <br /> <br /> If you have more charms than spare essence you can never have access to all your spent xp at once. I'd like to avoid that if possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T22:00:19-07:00","id":1229295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals#post1227167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To anyone who actually played an alchemical in 2E, how often did you actually swap out individual charms or entire charm arrays?<br /> <br /> I'm in the process of trying to convert our beloved robots to 3E but I realized that in practice the charm slot/attunement cost setup of 2E may not have been as modular/adaptable as the book makes it out to be.<br /> <br /> Please no speculation. I'd like actual play experience only. Context of what type of game you were playing would also be very helpful. I'm trying to get a sense of how modular alchemicals need to be in play and whether I need to create systems to encourage/smooth out charm swapping or not.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for any feedback!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not very often. Despite claims of adaptability Alchemical PC's I had across two long spanning games generally made a single large array for themselves. This is why I just included the cost discount by default in mine (plus no one liked combos anywho).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T22:47:03-07:00","id":1229307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1229295#post1229295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not very often. Despite claims of adaptability Alchemical PC's I had across two long spanning games generally made a single large array for themselves. This is why I just included the cost discount by default in mine (plus no one liked combos anywho).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for your input!<br /> <br /> Every little bit of info helps with the conversion!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T11:10:46-07:00","id":1229405,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not sure I agree with the idea. Largely because, once you\u2019ve bought, say, ten Evocations from four different charms, you\u2019ll probably never have to buy charms or Evocations again, or at least until your essence goes up. If you want different charms you just go swap them out.<br /> <br /> Personally, I\u2019d say that if it\u2019s fairly easy to swap them out when you really need to then it should be fine to charge xp for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T11:17:25-07:00","id":1229408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1229405#post1229405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not sure I agree with the idea. Largely because, once you\u2019ve bought, say, ten Evocations from four different charms, you\u2019ll probably never have to buy charms or Evocations again, or at least until your essence goes up. If you want different charms you just go swap them out.<br /> <br /> Personally, I\u2019d say that if it\u2019s fairly easy to swap them out when you really need to then it should be fine to charge xp for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>hmmm... this is true... I'll think on that as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T18:43:41-07:00","id":1229493,"title":"","content":"While access to every one of your charms is always nice, not having that feels like a very Alchemical thing. They balanced not having all the charms by making them dirt cheap. If an Alchemical can buy 2 charms for the price of one compared to all other Exalted, the ability to only use it half the time is a fair balance, and it was a unique thing to Alchemicals, much like Aura is now for DBs.<br /> <br /> Keep the charm purchase price cheap, 3 or 4 xp, and/or let it be bought with RP xp but not the installations you need to purchase.<br /> <br /> Keeping with the Evocation model, make them pay for each Alchemical Evocation, but make each one cost like 3xp vs 8xp of the great at it solars. Then if they switch out between two Alche charms sets, they had plenty of XP to purchase both to the level they need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T18:59:58-07:00","id":1229494,"title":"","content":"OH, additionally, since they are Attribute based, if all their 'parts/chakra points/zones' are collectively nine points, maybe they just improve each zone, easy to focus for all the generic excellencies they used to have, translated a bit looser, like dex installation holds the Graceful Crane equivalent charm.<br /> <br /> Big deal charms like piston hammer &amp; mind spike likely need their own installation if they get multi-attribute requirements. So not everything has to fit the base 9 set-up now that i think about it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T19:12:56-07:00","id":1229496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cryo-Seraph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1227167-a-question-about-2e-alchemicals?p=1229494#post1229494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OH, additionally, since they are Attribute based, if all their 'parts/chakra points/zones' are collectively nine points, maybe they just improve each zone, easy to focus for all the generic excellencies they used to have, translated a bit looser, like dex installation holds the Graceful Crane equivalent charm.<br /> <br /> Big deal charms like piston hammer &amp; mind spike likely need their own installation if they get multi-attribute requirements. So not everything has to fit the base 9 set-up now that i think about it</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I'm going to go with the attribute basis actually. Their excellencies will be attribute based but otherwise the charms themselves will be material based. Literally a caste and a favoured magical material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T19:46:52-07:00","id":1229710,"title":"","content":"If we are proposing other options:<br /> <br /> What if an Assembly can share charms but only install charms from others in general slots which cost more than dedicated?<br /> Correlary: All Vats have a stock of spare charms you can install in general slots.<br /> <br /> You buy evocation &quot;upgrades&quot; on a per slot basis and they are expensive. So you could buy up one slot to have a bunch of evocations/submods but would have only basic functionality in all your other trees.<br /> <br /> Each &quot;charm&quot; is actually a mini charmset with evocations/submods and the number of slots and charms is sharply limited. You could use the artifacts are all unique to allow players to &quot;customize&quot; their example. So your PDMH might have plasma jets owing to its red jade while mine has health drain because of its soulsteel.<br /> Possible Correlary: Charms are mixed material but evocations/submods do have material much like the mixed element DB trees. This affects install/attune cost. Perhaps you favor your base material and can favor another?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}